 "stdout": "--- step 1: tool call (261 tokens) ---\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import fsolve, newton\n\n# Define the function f(x) = x^x - 10\ndef f(x):\n    return x**x - 10\n\n# Use fsolve to find the root\nx = fsolve(f, 2.0)[0]  # Initial guess of 2.0\nprint(f\"x = {x}\")\nprint(f\"x^x = {x**x}\")\n\n# Verify the solution\nprint(f\"Check: x^x = {x**x}\")\nprint(f\"Difference from 10: {abs(x**x - 10)}\")\n--- output ---\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 1, in <module>\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'numpy'\n--- step 2: tool call (377 tokens) ---\nimport math\n\n# Define the function f(x) = x^x - 10\ndef f(x):\n    return x**x - 10\n\n# Use Newton's method to find the root\ndef newton_method(f, df, x0, tol=1e-15, max_iter=100):\n    x = x0\n    for i in range(max_iter):\n        fx = f(x)\n        if abs(fx) < tol:\n            return x\n        dfx = df(x)\n        if dfx == 0:\n            break\n        x_new = x - fx / dfx\n        if abs(x_new - x) < tol:\n            return x_new\n        x = x_new\n    return x\n\n# Derivative of x^x - 10\ndef df(x):\n    # d/dx(x^x) = x^x * (1 + ln(x))\n    return x**x * (1 + math.log(x))\n\n# Initial guess\nx = newton_method(f, df, 2.0)\nprint(f\"x = {x}\")\nprint(f\"x^x = {x**x}\")\nprint(f\"Difference from 10: {abs(x**x - 10)}\")\n\n# Round to 10 decimal places\nprint(f\"x rounded to 10 decimal places: {round(x, 10)}\")\n--- output ---\nx = 2.5061841455887692\nx^x = 10.0\nDifference from 10: 0.0\nx rounded to 10 decimal places: 2.5061841456\n--- step 3: tool call (191 tokens) ---\nx = 2.5061841456\nprint(f\"x^x = {x**x}\")\nprint(f\"Difference from 10: {abs(x**x - 10)}\")\nprint(f\"Rounded to 10 decimal places: {round(x, 10)}\")\n--- output ---\nx^x = 10.000000000215488\nDifference from 10: 2.1548807183080498e-10\nRounded to 10 decimal places: 2.5061841456\n--- step 4: final answer (finish=stop, 201 tokens) ---\n\n\nThe solution to the equation $x^x = 10$ is:\n\n**x = 2.506